After writing it, RUN it once with that command and fix errors until it exports every piece. Then look at the preview PNG and fix anything that reads badly.
Read `Art/tools/specs/_ch4_common.md` first (material names, richness, bevel, export settings). Use `Art/tools/blender_kit_ch4_weapons.py` as the style / export reference (same FBX settings).

## Goal
The ELITE (powered-up) version of the chapter-4 "Pendulum Knight" enemy. The game re-uses the normal knight's rigged body and bolts these extra ARMOR PIECES onto its bones, plus a bigger main weapon, so it reads clearly stronger, heavier, rustier.
The knight is a chunky 2-head-tall clockwork armored doll. Measurements for a **2.2 m tall** knight (design every piece at this scale; the game scales them with the body):
- helmet head: centre about Z 1.85, radius ~0.32 (top of helmet Z ~2.15, a red plume already sticks up from the top)
- shoulder joint: X 짹0.27, Z 1.42 ; torso is ~0.75 wide and ~0.6 deep (Y -0.3 .. +0.3) at the chest, chest front surface at about Y +0.30
- hips joint Z 1.06, belt at Z ~1.05 front at Y +0.30
- a wind-up key already sticks out of the back.
Look and feel (from the concept art): rusted heavy plate armour, layered spiked pauldrons with a swirl relief, brass gears rising behind the shoulders, a pendulum rod + round bob hanging on the chest, a long kite-shaped front tasset with a diamond inlay, gear-tooth hems, rivets everywhere, torn red cloth accents. Noir palette: dark iron + bright silver plates + brass gears, red only as accent (`red_lacquer`, `red_dark`, `gem_red`, `ribbon_red`). Use rust-ish `copper`/`brass_dark` flecks as small inset patches.

Coordinates for every piece: Blender Z-up, **+Y = the knight's FRONT**, **+X = the knight's RIGHT side** (the knight faces +Y). Each piece's ORIGIN is the ATTACH POINT given below (the game puts the origin on that bone), NOT the bottom centre.
Each piece = ONE joined mesh, exported to `Game/Assets/Art/Characters/Ch4/Kit_KP_<Name>.fbx` (the main weapon to `Kit_W_PendulumScythePlus.fbx`). At least 4 materials per piece, bevels on hard edges, no detail thinner than ~0.03 m, chunky toy proportions, cel-shade friendly. Under ~4000 triangles each (weapon ~5000).

## Pieces
1. `Pauldron_R` ??origin = right shoulder joint. A huge layered pauldron sitting ON TOP of and outside the shoulder: dome ~0.55 wide (X) x 0.5 deep (Y) x 0.32 tall, its centre at (+0.12, 0, +0.14) from the origin, covering from X -0.05 to +0.40. Three overlapping lames stepping down outward, `silver` plates with `iron_dark` underlayers, a raised swirl relief (spiral ridge) on the top plate in `steel`, a row of `brass` rivets on each edge, 3 jagged spikes pointing outward/down along the lower edge in `silver`. Behind it (Y -0.15 .. -0.25) a `brass` gear (diameter 0.42, 10 teeth, 4 spokes, `brass_dark` hub) standing upright, rising so its top is ~0.30 above the dome. Small torn `ribbon_red` cloth strip hanging from the front edge (0.25 long).
2. `Pauldron_L` ??exact mirror of `Pauldron_R` across X (origin = left shoulder joint, piece extends to -X).
